# 
# https://github.com/tibonto/educor#EducationalResource
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#EducationalResource> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#EducationalResource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EducationalResource"@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#EducationalResource> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Any educational resources online or offline"@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#EducationalResource> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A video describing how lists work in Python programming language"@en .
# 
# https://github.com/tibonto/educor#KnowledgeTopic
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#KnowledgeTopic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#KnowledgeTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://purl.org/ontology/modalia#Skill> .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#KnowledgeTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "KnowledgeTopic"@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#KnowledgeTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> "https://w3id.org/ccso/ccso#Topic"@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#KnowledgeTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A single node representing a learning module based on the domain ontology. It contains all the learning material for the specific learning module."@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#KnowledgeTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A knowledge topic can be the “Quadratic equations” in the domain of Mathematics Algebra"@en .
# 
# https://github.com/tibonto/educor#LearningPath
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#LearningPath> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#LearningPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Often here it is mapped the background knowledge too."@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#LearningPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LearningPath"@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#LearningPath> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The learning path consists of learner's previously followed topics and future ones in order to reach to the learning goal. It is an ordered list of recommendations, which is personalized to the needs of a certain user and target the accomplishment of a complex skill. It has as a final point a learning goal."@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#LearningPath> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "\"Hello world in python\", \"Comments in python\", \"Strings in python\""@en .
# 
# https://github.com/tibonto/educor#LearningPreference
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#LearningPreference> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#LearningPreference> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "It is based on the theory which identifies four learning styles (visual, auditory, reading, and kinesthetic)."@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#LearningPreference> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LearningPreference"@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#LearningPreference> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The learning preference of the user based on the learning styles theory"@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#LearningPreference> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Visual"@en .
# 
# https://github.com/tibonto/educor#Question
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#Question> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#Question> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Question"@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#Question> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Part of an exercise. A test has one or many exercises and therefore questions. An exercise can have multiple questions too"@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#Question> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "\"What is the solution to the equation ln(x-3)=0 ?\"" .
# 
# https://github.com/tibonto/educor#Recommendation
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#Recommendation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#Recommendation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The recommendation in advanced systems can also be an action (take a small break), an exercise, a knowledge topic, a skill, or a learning path"@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#Recommendation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Recommendation"@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#Recommendation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The output of the recommendation system algorithm. The system that reads user profile, content information, ratings and any available rules, in order to generate a meaningful recommendation."@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#Recommendation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The recommendation is \"Quadratic Equation\""@en .
# 
# https://github.com/tibonto/educor#UserLogs
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#UserLogs> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#UserLogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "UserLogs"@en .
<https://github.com/tibonto/educor#UserLogs> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The user's history activity in the system"@en .
